---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { getHreflangStaticPaths } from "../lib/hreflang-helpers";
import { localePath } from "../utils/base";
import { t } from "../i18n/ui";
import { EDITOR, LEGAL_UPDATED } from "../config/legal";
import type { Locale } from "../i18n/config";

const locale: Locale = "en";
const lp = (path: string) => localePath(path, locale);
const h2 = "font-display text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3";
const link = "text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-800 font-medium";
---

<Layout title="Terms of Use | WizyQuiz, Free Online Quizzes" description="The rules for using WizyQuiz: free access to quizzes, player accounts, quizzes created by players, games with friends and liability." locale={locale} hreflangPaths={getHreflangStaticPaths("terms")}>
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-gray-500 mb-8" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href={lp("/")} class="hover:text-brand-600 transition-colors font-medium">{t(locale, "breadcrumb.home")}</a>
      <svg class="w-3 h-3 text-gray-300" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
      <span class="text-gray-700 font-semibold">Terms of Use</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-8">Terms of Use</h1>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-700">
      <section>
        <h2 class={h2}>1. Purpose</h2>
        <p>These terms set out the rules for using WizyQuiz (https://wizyquiz.com), published by {EDITOR.name}. By using the site, you accept them. They cost nobody anything: the site is free, with no subscription and no purchases.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={h2}>2. The service</h2>
        <p>WizyQuiz offers general knowledge quizzes in six game modes (multiple choice, true or false, chrono challenge, estimation, duel, chronological order), mini-games, games with friends using a code, and a tool for creating your own quizzes. Every quiz can be played without an account. A free account also lets you keep your history, earn XP, add friends and save the quizzes you create.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">The site may change, be interrupted for maintenance or close, and since the service is free, this does not give rise to any compensation.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={h2}>3. Player accounts</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
          <li>You must be 15 or older, or have a parent's consent, to create an account.</li>
          <li>The email address you give must be your own. Your password is personal, so don't share it.</li>
          <li>Your username is visible to other players. It must not be offensive or impersonate someone else.</li>
          <li>You can delete your account at any time from your profile ("Delete my account"). The account and everything linked to it are then erased.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={h2}>4. Quizzes created by players</h2>
        <p>Each quiz created gets a link that its author can share with anyone they like. It is not reviewed, not shown in the catalog and not indexed by search engines. Its author is responsible for it and agrees not to publish anything in it that is:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 mt-2">
          <li>illegal, defamatory, offensive, hateful or discriminatory;</li>
          <li>pornographic or violent;</li>
          <li>copied from someone else's work without the right to use it (texts, images);</li>
          <li>used for advertising or spam.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">By publishing a quiz, the author allows WizyQuiz to host it and show it to people who have the link, free of charge and for as long as the quiz exists. The author can delete it at any time from "My quizzes". A quiz that breaks these rules may be deleted without notice. To report one, write to {EDITOR.email} with its link.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={h2}>5. Games with friends</h2>
        <p>A room can be created without an account, with just a nickname, and it disappears after six hours. The nickname is visible to every player in the room, and the same rules apply as for a username.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={h2}>6. Fair use of the site</h2>
        <p>You may not try to disrupt the site (attacks, sending large volumes of requests, automated scraping of the content), get around its protections or rig the leaderboards. In case of abuse, access can be blocked and the account deleted.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={h2}>7. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>The quizzes, texts, logo and code of the site belong to {EDITOR.name}, as explained in the <a href={lp("/legal-notices")} class={link}>legal notices</a>. You are free to share the link to a quiz, but copying the questions elsewhere requires permission.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={h2}>8. Liability</h2>
        <p>The quizzes are there to play and to learn. A mistake can slip into a question: report it to {EDITOR.email} and it will be corrected. WizyQuiz is not responsible for the content of quizzes created by players, or for the sites that any external links point to.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={h2}>9. Personal data</h2>
        <p>What is collected and your rights are described in the <a href={lp("/privacy-policy")} class={link}>privacy policy</a> and on the <a href={lp("/cookies")} class={link}>cookies</a> page.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={h2}>10. Changes</h2>
        <p>These terms may be updated, and the date at the bottom of the page will change when they are.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={h2}>11. Governing law and disputes</h2>
        <p>These terms are governed by French law. If there is a disagreement, write to {EDITOR.email} first so that an amicable solution can be found. Failing that, the competent court can be referred to, including the court where you live if you are a consumer.</p>
      </section>

      <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 pt-4 border-t border-gray-200">Last updated: {LEGAL_UPDATED.en}</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
